# Testing Standards

## Coverage Requirements
- Critical domains (service orders, stock, budget) must have minimum 90% test coverage
- All other domains require minimum 80% coverage
- Coverage is measured on: statements, branches, functions, lines

## What Must Be Tested
### Unit Tests
- Service order status transition logic: valid transitions, invalid transitions, REJECTED terminal state
- Budget calculation: services only, parts only, combined, zero items
- CPF validation: valid CPF, invalid format, invalid digits, edge cases
- CNPJ validation: valid CNPJ, invalid format, invalid digits, edge cases
- License plate validation: old format, Mercosul format, invalid formats
- Stock decrement: success path, out-of-stock error, concurrent access guard
- JWT generation and validation logic
- RBAC: ADMIN exclusive role enforcement, multi-role assignment, 403 on out-of-scope access
- Customer creation triggers User creation with role CLIENT and hashed default password
- Customer deletion triggers User deletion/deactivation

### Integration Tests
- POST /service-orders — create service order, verify status is RECEIVED, verify budget is calculated
- PATCH /service-orders/:id/status — advance each status step, test invalid transitions return 422
- POST /service-orders/:id/approve — CLIENT role approves own budget, verify status moves to IN_PROGRESS
- POST /service-orders/:id/reject — CLIENT role rejects own budget, verify status becomes REJECTED
- POST /service-orders/:id/approve — returns 403 when called with ADMIN/ATTENDANT/MECHANIC role
- Stock decrement on part association: verify DB quantity decreases in same transaction
- GET /service-orders/:id/status — public endpoint, no auth, returns current status
- Admin endpoints return 401 without JWT, 200 with valid JWT
- MECHANIC role returns 403 on customer/user management endpoints
- CLIENT role returns 403 when accessing other customers' service orders
- CLIENT role filtered by customerId: cannot approve/reject service orders of another customer
- POST /users — only ADMIN can create ADMIN users; ATTENDANT attempt returns 403
- PUT /users/:id/roles — only ADMIN can change roles; others return 403

## Test Structure
- Arrange / Act / Assert pattern for all tests
- Each test must be independent — no shared mutable state between tests
- Use test doubles (mocks/stubs) at service layer boundaries in unit tests
- Integration tests must use a real (test) database, rolled back after each test
- Test file names mirror source file names with `.test` or `.spec` suffix

## Naming Convention
- Test description must clearly state: what is being tested, the input condition, expected outcome
- Example: `"should throw OUT_OF_STOCK error when part quantity is zero"`
- Example: `"should return 403 when MECHANIC attempts to delete a customer"`
- Group related tests with describe blocks named after the unit under test
